00:23:56.792 --> 00:24:00.750
Gary, how do you define
the grind versus the hustle,

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:05.000
and Coffee, how do you define
Matty, how do you define

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:08.250
inspiration versus motivation,
what's the difference?

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:09.625
- You start.

00:24:09.625 --> 00:24:12.125
- Inspiration versus motivation.

00:24:12.125 --> 00:24:16.500
I think, to inspire,

00:24:16.500 --> 00:24:19.542
inspiration can come from
just words you can pick up

00:24:19.542 --> 00:24:24.083
on Google, and just put
them up and inspire people.

00:24:24.083 --> 00:24:28.291
To motivate people is
to get involved, you know,

00:24:28.291 --> 00:24:33.291
one of the things I did
in 2010, that's the year

00:24:33.291 --> 00:24:36.917
South Africa was
hosting World Cup.

00:24:36.917 --> 00:24:40.125
I started a
DJ Black Coffee foundation

00:24:40.125 --> 00:24:43.250
and the launch of it,

00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:46.708
because I wanted
to motivate people

00:24:46.708 --> 00:24:50.291
I set up a stage in
the middle of Soweto,

00:24:51.417 --> 00:24:55.583
in a shopping center and
DJ'ed for 60 hours like,

00:24:57.625 --> 00:25:02.166
from Thursday
midnight until Sunday midday.

00:25:02.166 --> 00:25:05.625
That was motivation,
you know, for me that's the

00:25:05.625 --> 00:25:10.333
difference between motivating
someone and inspiring someone.

00:25:10.333 --> 00:25:13.834
I used that as a motivation
and I kept saying in interviews

00:25:13.834 --> 00:25:17.542
when we were building up
to it, I want people to see

00:25:17.542 --> 00:25:22.750
what I'm doing, and get
up and do something similar.

00:25:22.750 --> 00:25:25.542
There's so many different
homes with people that are

00:25:25.542 --> 00:25:29.083
in need in South Africa,
go there, spend a day,

00:25:29.083 --> 00:25:32.625
do laundry, cook for them,
this is what I was trying to do

00:25:32.625 --> 00:25:35.959
to motivate them to
get up and do something,

00:25:35.959 --> 00:25:40.166
that's how I think
I define the two.

00:25:40.166 --> 00:25:42.917
- It's so crazy, I've never
DJ'ed in my entire life,

00:25:42.917 --> 00:25:44.333
when he was talking I was like,

00:25:44.333 --> 00:25:46.291
I'm going to
fucking DJ for 61 hours

00:25:46.291 --> 00:25:47.458
(audience laughter)

00:25:47.458 --> 00:25:51.208
I'm so sick, I'm like
such a broken person, anyway.

00:25:51.208 --> 00:25:53.750
I actually am gonna use this
opportunity to do something

00:25:53.750 --> 00:25:55.834
